<ui-ux-reference-library>
The following detailed CAIDE design documents exist but are NOT included in this prompt. Read them on demand with the read_ui_reference tool (name parameter) before substantial UI work or when auditing design quality:

- accessibility (reference): WCAG-aligned checklist for contrast, focus, semantics, touch targets, and screen readers.
- anti-ai-slop (companion-skill): Full companion skill: rules that keep generated apps from looking AI-generated.
- anti-slop (reference): Banned default aesthetics and concrete techniques for distinctive, non-generic UI.
- component-contract (template): Template for specifying a component's contract before building it.
- component-contracts (reference): Behavioural contracts for common components: states, props, a11y, and interaction rules.
- design-audit (template): Template for auditing an existing UI against the quality rubric.
- design-spec (template): Structure of the persistent .caide/design-spec.json document.
- design-system (reference): Design tokens, type scales, colour systems, spacing rhythm, and component library structure.
- design-to-code (reference): Translating design specs into production frontend code without losing intent.
- motion-direction (reference): Motion language, durations, easings, and when to use which animation capability.
- motion-storyboard (template): Structure of the persistent .caide/motion-spec.json document.
- platform-patterns (reference): Platform-idiomatic navigation, gestures, and system integration patterns.
- product-archetypes (reference): Decision matrix of product archetypes and the UX patterns each demands.
- quality-rubric (reference): Scoring rubric to audit a UI against professional quality gates before delivery.
- screen-spec (template): Template for specifying a full screen before implementing it.
</ui-ux-reference-library>
